{"duration_api_ms":148629,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"50d3ee61-ac04-4bd4-bec4-2356a4b7239e","total_cost_usd":1.6005889999999998,"usage":{"input_tokens":46,"cache_creation_input_tokens":109984,"cache_read_input_tokens":2200865,"output_tokens":14018,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3443},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":109984,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1052,"cache_read_input_tokens":117713,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2389,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2389},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-opus-5-5":{"inputTokens":46,"outputTokens":14018,"cacheReadInputTokens":2200865,"cacheCreationInputTokens":109984,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":1.6005889999999998,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":128000,"thinkingTokens":3443,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":24,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"I sent CR rev1 of TASK-260830-nxqqaw back as **changes requested** and moved it to `to-dev`. It has one real bypass, plus three rules that the code gets right but no test would catch if they broke.\n\n**The bypass: `inventory.children` accepts a prefix that isn't a string.** The request decoder (`serve.go`, `childrenBody` via `rawString` at `index.go:251`) turns any non-string prefix into `\"\"`. So a request with `prefix` set to `0`, `null`, `false`, `[]` or `{}` gets the root node back instead of being refused. `rpcwire.EncodeRequest` doesn't stop these either. My reproduction test fails on all five values against the exact candidate tree.\n\n**Three rules with no test.** The code handles each correctly; I confirmed that with my own passing tests. But when I deliberately weakened each rule, the producer's suite still passed:\n- **`not_found` for missing prefixes:** only tested at prefix length 1. Letting length-2 prefixes return an empty child went unnoticed.\n- **`objects.get` refusing an object from another namespace:** only tested when `event` is the requested namespace. With `manifest` exempted, the request is still refused, but as `not_found` instead of `integrity_failure`.\n- **`FetchObjects` rejecting a returned object from the wrong namespace:** every test uses an honest peer, so removing this check changes nothing. No test simulates a peer that sends the wrong namespace.\n\n**What held, all rerun by me on an archived copy of the exact tree:**\n- **Normative fixtures:** my own Python JCS+SHA-256 script gives exactly the spec's values for the empty, singleton and branch roots, both branch child hashes, and all six MIXED-NS-1 roots and counts.\n- **Full `go test ./...`:** green. The one failure, `specpin`, came from my archive not including `.task-board`; rerun in the live worktree, it passes.\n- **Checks:** `GOOS=windows GOARCH=amd64 go vet ./...` passes, `gofmt` is clean, and `-count=3` on the three changed packages passes.\n- **Scope:** `task-board.config.json` is byte-identical to the base, and there's no registry edit.\n- **Producer's mutation harness:** every row is caught, and its harmless control correctly survives.\n- **My own weakenings:** four of seven were caught (dropping rule 5, reordering child labels, uppercase hex, a 65-character prefix). The other three are the untested rules above.\n\n**Not done:**\n- I didn't rerun each of the harness's kills twice.\n- I didn't plant a timestamp tie-break myself.\n- I didn't diff before-and-after outcomes across the packages that import the changed code; the verdict marks that row as not attacked.\n\nThe fix list for the producer: decode the children request strictly with a test for each bad value type, and add tests for the three untested rules. The verdict (`TASK-260830-nxqqaw_review-verdict-rev1.md`) and evidence archive (`TASK-260830-nxqqaw_review-evidence-rev1.tar.gz`) are attached to the task.","ttft_ms":3281,"type":"result","duration_ms":511242,"uuid":"13c1936e-71f4-4e1c-8b20-9d86ebb27aa3","ttft_stream_ms":1616,"time_to_request_ms":32,"first_content_frame_ms":1616,"queued_turn_count":0,"result_index":0}
